WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.269
Pinocchio and his new friends had lots of fun at Paradisle.

2
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:10.286
They ate ice cream for breakfast, played games all afternoon, and stayed up as late as they wanted.

3
00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:13.334
Every day really was a holiday.

4
00:00:13.335 --> 00:00:17.888
They had so much fun that they forgot how long they had been at Paradisle.

5
00:00:17.889 --> 00:00:21.571
They even forgot about their homes and families.

6
00:00:21.572 --> 00:00:25.245
For the first time, Pinocchio felt like a real boy.

7
00:00:25.246 --> 00:00:28.042
But he knew that he was still made of wood.

8
00:00:28.043 --> 00:00:32.497
So every night, he would look in the mirror, hoping to see a change.

9
00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:36.014
One night, when he looked in the mirror, he saw a change.

10
00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:38.705
But it was not the kind of change he wanted.

11
00:00:38.706 --> 00:00:40.902
He was covered in fur!

12
00:00:40.903 --> 00:00:43.715
Just then, there was a knock at the door.

13
00:00:43.716 --> 00:00:48.249
"Pinocchio, let me in!" cried one of his friends.

14
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.278
Pinocchio didn’t want anyone to see his fur.

15
00:00:51.279 --> 00:00:53.746
"Uh, I’m not here now.

16
00:00:53.747 --> 00:00:56.788
Come back later," he said.

17
00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:01.918
"Pinocchio, I know you’re in there because you are talking," said the boy.

18
00:01:01.919 --> 00:01:04.737
"Now let me in—hurry!"

19
00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:08.414
Pinocchio opened the door, and there stood his friend.

20
00:01:08.415 --> 00:01:10.471
He was covered in fur too!

21
00:01:10.472 --> 00:01:15.071
"Pinocchio, you have to help me!" the boy cried.

22
00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:18.412
"Help you? I don’t know how to help you!

23
00:01:18.413 --> 00:01:22.779
Look at me, I’m furry too!" said Pinocchio.

24
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:26.014
Both boys sat on the floor and began to cry.

25
00:01:26.015 --> 00:01:30.193
But, when they cried, they sounded like donkeys instead of boys:

26
00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:33.983
"Hee-haw, hee-haw!"

27
00:01:33.984 --> 00:01:37.504
Just then, there was another knock on the door.

28
00:01:37.505 --> 00:01:42.225
"Boys, are you all right in there?" the wagon master asked.

29
00:01:42.226 --> 00:01:44.551
The wagon master was their friend.

30
00:01:44.552 --> 00:01:46.757
He had brought them to Paradisle.

31
00:01:46.758 --> 00:01:48.843
He would know what to do.

32
00:01:48.844 --> 00:01:52.465
"Please, help us," they called.

33
00:01:52.466 --> 00:01:58.820
But it sounded like "Hee-haw, hee-haw."

34
00:01:58.821 --> 00:02:04.288
When the wagon master saw the boys, his smile turned to an evil laugh.

35
00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:12.554
"Ha-ha-ha! Now, it is time for you to pay for your play," he said.

36
00:02:12.555 --> 00:02:16.550
"For months, you have eaten and played without work.

37
00:02:16.551 --> 00:02:23.941
Now, you will become donkeys and work for me the rest of your lives!"

38
00:02:23.942 --> 00:02:27.589
"Donkeys?" the boys cried together.

39
00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:35.005
"But sir," said Pinocchio, "I don’t want to be a donkey, I want to be a real boy."

40
00:02:35.006 --> 00:02:37.981
When the wagon master heard this, he laughed.

41
00:02:37.982 --> 00:02:44.288
"A real boy? All you are going to be is a real donkey."

42
00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:49.514
He quickly tied a rope around the boys’ necks and led them to the ferry.

43
00:02:49.515 --> 00:02:54.270
The two boys tried to call for help, but their friends did not hear.

44
00:02:54.271 --> 00:02:57.032
They did not look like boys anymore.

45
00:02:57.033 --> 00:03:00.197
They looked like donkeys.

46
00:03:00.198 --> 00:03:05.420
"I will sell one of you to a farmer and the other of you to the circus.

47
00:03:05.421 --> 00:03:08.929
The circus will love a talking donkey.

48
00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:19.453
Pinocchio, I think you will make a good circus donkey since you like talking so much!" the man said, laughing.

49
00:03:19.454 --> 00:03:22.164
He led the two donkeys onto the ferry.

50
00:03:22.165 --> 00:03:25.672
There were many other sad-looking donkeys inside.

51
00:03:25.673 --> 00:03:31.773
Now, Pinocchio understood why he had seen so many donkeys that first day.

52
00:03:31.774 --> 00:03:37.926
He and all the other donkeys began to cry.

